## 3. Architecture Overview
<!-- ID: architecture_overview -->
### Component flow

1. The existing `handle_manage_docs_request` completes a successful mutation preview.
2. A shared issuer in `doc_management.apply_preview` captures the server-normalized intent plus an action-specific binding/precondition snapshot and persists it through `StorageBackend`.
3. Runtime attaches only the compact `apply` affordance before the create early return or common final return.
4. `apply_preview` validates its receipt-only input, claims the durable row atomically, rechecks current authority and state, executes the retained intent through the normal mutation path, verifies after-state, and stores a terminal result.
5. Retries return stored terminal output or a stable busy/recovery result without a second mutation.

### Seam map and dependency DAG

The Q2 shape is seven implementation/validation subsystems plus release, more than twelve owned files, more than two frozen contracts, and three waves. The dispatched contract requires a single planning pass, so this guide records the seam map and detailed packages together.

| Subsystem | Sole ownership | Provides | Depends on |
|---|---|---|---|
| SS-CONTRACT | receipt records and `StorageBackend` API | C-RECEIPT-STORAGE | none |
| SS-SQLITE | SQLite table and atomic methods | C-SQLITE-PARITY | SS-CONTRACT |
| SS-POSTGRES | PostgreSQL DDL/migration and atomic methods | C-POSTGRES-PARITY | SS-CONTRACT |
| SS-REMOTE | remote client/server operation parity | C-REMOTE-PARITY | SS-CONTRACT |
| SS-ENGINE | issuance, claim/replay orchestration, multi-path locks | C-APPLY-ENGINE | SS-CONTRACT and all backends |
| SS-RUNTIME | public action, automatic affordance, composite rehome executor | C-PUBLIC-APPLY and C-REHOME-COMPOSITE | SS-ENGINE and completed rehome baseline |
| SS-VALIDATE | end-to-end parity and security evidence | evidence receipts | all implementation |
| SS-RELEASE | 2.14.0 version/readme truth | release artifact | validation |

DAG layers are `[SS-CONTRACT]`, `[SS-SQLITE, SS-POSTGRES, SS-REMOTE]`, `[SS-ENGINE]`, `[SS-RUNTIME]`, `[SS-VALIDATE]`, `[SS-RELEASE]`.

I1: active package ownership is pairwise disjoint; the completed baseline package is historical, and `SCRIBE-REHOME-B3` remains the single live owner of dirty runtime/rehome files. I2: the layers above are acyclic. I3: every named cross-subsystem contract has one producer. I4: each subsystem maps to one package and owns no more than six files. I5: contract surfaces are concrete in Detailed Design. I6: the union covers the SPEC change surface; prompts, rosters, skills, generated outputs, deployment, Git delivery, and unrelated code are explicitly outside it.


